id: 't13p2', test: 13, part: 2, title: 'Open day at a community garden', titleVi: 'Buổi giới thiệu ngày hội mở cửa vườn cộng đồng', topic: 'Community & environment', level: 'B1+',
context: 'The coordinator of a community garden briefs volunteers before the garden’s annual open day.',
speakers: { A: { name: 'Ruth (garden coordinator)', accent: 'en-GB', gender: 'f' } },
script: [
{ say: 'Part 2. You will hear the coordinator of a community garden talking to volunteers about its open day. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.' }, { pause: 4 },
{ s: 'A', t: "Hello, everyone, and thank you for coming. I'm Ruth, the coordinator here at Larkfield Community Garden, and I'm very grateful that so many of you have offered to help with Saturday's open day." },
{ s: 'A', t: "I know some of you have been volunteering for years, while others have only just joined, so I'll try to make sure that everybody leaves this meeting knowing exactly what to expect." },
{ s: 'A', t: "For those of you who are new, let me say a little about how the garden began. Ten years ago, this whole area was a disused bowling green. The council was about to sell it for building land, but a group of neighbours persuaded them to lease it to us instead." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Over the years we've added a lot. The greenhouse, for example, is our proudest achievement. Most of the money for it was raised at our annual plant sale. The council grant that we received last year only paid for the new fencing." },
{ s: 'A', t: "We now have sixty plots, and members rent a plot for one year at a time. There's a long waiting list, so if you hear someone say they're hoping to get one, please don't promise them anything." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Our gardeners come from every part of the neighbourhood. We have a retired bus driver who grows the biggest pumpkins I've ever seen, a family who share one plot between three generations, and a group of students who experiment with vegetables from all over the world. That mixture is what makes the garden special, and I'd like visitors on Saturday to feel it." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Now, Saturday. We're expecting around five hundred visitors, which is far more than we've ever had. The biggest problem will be parking. Elm Road is very narrow and the residents have already complained, so we're asking everyone to park at the primary school, which has kindly opened its playground for the day. It's only a five-minute walk." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Some people have suggested a shuttle bus, but it would cost too much and we'd need a driver, so we've decided against it. We're encouraging people to cycle if they can, and there'll be bike racks by the entrance." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Please be polite to anyone who asks you about the traffic. Our neighbours have been very patient with us over the years, and we'd like to keep it that way. If a resident does complain, don't argue. Just take their name, and I'll call them on Monday." },
{ s: 'A', t: "As for you, the volunteers, I'd like you all here by nine. No, sorry, I need to correct that. Half past eight, because the stalls take longer to set up than you'd think. There'll be tea and toast for everyone. You'll each be given a green apron so visitors can easily recognise you." },
{ s: 'A', t: "During the day, you'll work in shifts of about two hours, so that nobody gets tired. If you need a break, there are chairs by the shed, and a first-aid kit is kept in the hall. Please remember to drink plenty of water, even if it rains." },
{ pause: 1.5 },
{ say: g.LTI[6] }, { pause: 3 },
{ s: 'A', t: "Now let me explain where everything will be. Have a look at the plan of the garden on your sheet. As visitors come in through the main gate, they'll find the registration table straight away, where we hand out leaflets. That's the only thing near the entrance, so we want the crowd to move on quickly." },
{ s: 'A', t: "The seed swap will be under the apple trees. People bring packets of seeds from their own gardens and swap them. It's the most popular activity every year, so I've given it the biggest space, with plenty of shade." },
{ s: 'A', t: "The bee demonstration will take place behind the shed. Our beekeeper, Anil, will open a hive, and for safety visitors must stay behind a rope, so we need a quiet area away from the paths." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Next, the compost workshop. You might think compost isn't very exciting, but it always attracts a crowd. It'll be beside the greenhouse, because the heaps are right there." },
{ s: 'A', t: "The workshop is led by Mehmet, who has looked after our compost for six years. He promises to explain it without any difficult scientific words, and he usually gives away a small bag of the finished product to anyone who asks a good question." },
{ s: 'A', t: "The pond is a lovely spot, and people will want to look at it, but please don't put any stalls there. Frogs and small children don't mix well with crowds." },
{ s: 'A', t: "The children's den-building will be by the herb spiral. We've collected lots of branches and old sheets. It's near enough for parents to see, but away from the busy paths." },
{ s: 'A', t: "And finally, refreshments. We'll serve soup, cakes and hot drinks in the community hall, because the forecast says it might rain, and we'd like people to have somewhere dry to sit." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Everything on the menu is made from ingredients grown in the garden or donated by local shops, and the cakes are baked by our members. All the money raised goes into next year's seeds and tools." },
{ s: 'A', t: "One last thing. Please take photographs on the day, and send your favourites to the garden's email address afterwards. We use them for our newsletter, and they help us to persuade people to support us next year." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Visitors will also be able to buy plants from the stall at the gate, and every pot has a label explaining how to look after it. If anyone asks you for advice, don't be shy. Tell them what you know, and if you aren't sure, ask one of the experienced gardeners." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Right. If there are no questions, let's go and put up the signs." },


],
