script: [
{ say: 'Part 1. You will hear a man phoning the organiser of a craft fair to book a stall. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 6.' }, { pause: 4 },
{ s: 'A', t: "Good morning, Eastvale Craft Fair office. This is Nadia." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Hello, Nadia. My name is Callum Brennick, and I'd like to book a stall at this year's winter fair, if there is still space." },
{ s: 'A', t: "There is, but it's filling up quickly. I'll complete the application form as we talk. Could you spell your surname for me, please?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "Yes, it's B, R, E, N, N, I, C, K." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Thank you. And what's the name of your business?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "Bluebird Candles. I run it from my garage at home, and this will be my first time at a fair of this size, so I'm a little nervous." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Don't be. Most of our traders started small. What's the best number to reach you on?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "My mobile is oh seven eight nine six, double two one, double four seven." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Oh seven eight nine six, double two one, double four seven. Lovely. Now, what will you be selling? Our application form asks us to record the main product." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Last year I sold soap as well, but I've stopped making it because it took too much time. So this year it's handmade candles, and nothing else." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Candles are always popular at the winter fair. Now, about the size of your stall. We have a standard stall, which is three metres wide, and a double stall, which is six metres wide. There is nothing in between." },
{ s: 'B', t: "I was hoping for four metres, but I suppose that's not possible. I have a lot of stock and a display shelf, so the double stall sounds better. Six metres, please." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Six metres it is. We have two halls this year. The Harcourt Hall is for food and drink, and the Tamarind Hall is for crafts and gifts. As you make candles, you would be in the Tamarind Hall. That's T, A, M, A, R, I, N, D." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Thank you. I think I'll be in good company there." },
{ s: 'A', t: "You will. Do you need electricity at the stall? Some traders want lights or a card reader, and we include sockets in the price." },
{ s: 'B', t: "I'll need one for the lights, so one socket. Actually, I'll probably bring a card reader as well, so I'd better ask for two." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Two sockets, noted." },
{ pause: 1.5 },
{ say: g.LTI[3] }, { pause: 3 },
{ s: 'B', t: "What does the double stall cost?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "The standard stall is a hundred and forty pounds for the whole weekend. The double stall is two hundred and forty, which is a little less than twice as much, so it is good value." },
{ s: 'B', t: "That's reasonable. Does that include a table?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "I'm afraid not. You can bring your own, or hire tables from us at fifteen pounds each. Chairs are free, and we provide a banner with your business name." },
{ s: 'B', t: "I'll bring my own tables. When can I set up my stall?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Traders can enter the hall from half past seven on Saturday morning, and the doors open to the public at ten. Most people need at least an hour and a half to arrange everything, so please don't leave it late." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Understood. Half past seven it is. Is there anything to pay in advance?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Yes, we ask for a deposit to hold the space. For food traders it is fifty percent, because of the extra checks we have to carry out, but for craft stalls it is thirty percent of the stall fee, payable within a week." },
{ s: 'B', t: "That's fine. I can pay by card now, if you like." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Better to wait until you have the confirmation email, which I'll send this afternoon. It will include a plan of the hall and a parking pass for your van." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Wonderful. And if I have to cancel, is there a charge?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "You can cancel without charge up to a month before the fair, and after that we keep the deposit. Most traders never need to." },
{ s: 'B', t: "One more thing. Will there be much advertising for the fair? I'm hoping to attract customers who have never heard of my business." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Yes, we put posters in every library and café in the area, and there are adverts on local radio for the two weeks before. We also post a profile of each trader on our website, so please send me a short description of your business and two photographs of your candles by the end of next week." },
{ s: 'B', t: "I'll do that tonight. Should I mention that the candles are made from natural wax?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Definitely. Customers like to know how things are made, and it gives you something to talk about at the stall. Many of our visitors come back every year, and they enjoy meeting the people behind the products." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Good to know. Thank you very much, Nadia. I'm looking forward to it." },
{ s: 'A', t: "You're welcome, Callum. Welcome to the fair, and good luck with the candles." },
],
