script: [
{ say: 'Part 1. You will hear a man phoning a photography studio to book a photographer for his wedding. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 6.' }, { pause: 4 },
{ s: 'A', t: "Good afternoon, Fennel Row Photography, Joanne speaking. How can I help?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "Hello. My fiancée and I are getting married in the autumn, and we'd like to find out whether you still have a photographer free." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Congratulations! We may well have. I'll open the booking form on my screen and take some details as we go. Could I have your surname, please?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "It's Haldane. That's H, A, L, D, A, N, E." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Thank you, Mr Haldane. And which date have you set for the wedding?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "The fourteenth of September. We were lucky to get a Saturday." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Lovely. Ah, I'm afraid the fourteenth is already taken. Both of our senior photographers are booked that day." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Oh no. Well, the register office did say there was a free slot the week after, so we could move everything. Would the twenty-first be possible?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Let me check. Yes, the twenty-first is free, and Ross, our most experienced photographer, is available. Shall I put you down for that?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "Please do. I'll tell my fiancée tonight, but I'm sure she'll agree." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Now, where will you be holding the reception? That helps us to plan the lighting, because indoor and outdoor venues are very different." },
{ s: 'B', t: "It's at Heron Barn, just outside the village of Leyton. The ceremony itself is at the register office in town at two o'clock, and then everyone drives out to the barn." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Heron Barn is beautiful, and Ross has worked there before. How many guests are you expecting?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "At first we invited a hundred and twenty, but quite a few people have said no, so I think it will be eighty-five. That is the number the caterers are working with, anyway." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Eighty-five. Good. And what sort of photographs do you have in mind? Some couples like formal pictures with everyone lined up, and others prefer something more relaxed." },
{ s: 'B', t: "My parents would love a few formal group photographs, and we'll certainly have those. But personally I dislike stiff poses. I'd much rather have natural pictures of people laughing and chatting, the kind where nobody realises the camera is there." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Candid photography is Ross's speciality, so you're in good hands. I'll make a note that candid shots are the priority, with half an hour set aside for the formal ones." },
{ s: 'B', t: "That sounds perfect." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Finally for this part, a contact number, please." },
{ s: 'B', t: "My mobile is oh double seven double oh, nine one three, four six zero." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Sorry, was that four six zero at the end?" },
{ s: 'B', t: "No, I'm sorry, I said it wrongly. It ends four six two." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Four six two. Thank you. I've got everything I need for the form." },
{ pause: 1.5 },
{ say: g.LTI[3] }, { pause: 3 },
{ s: 'B', t: "Could you tell me about your packages? I saw three on your website, but I'm not sure which would suit us." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Of course. The Bronze package is four hours of coverage, which is really only enough for the ceremony and a few pictures afterwards. Silver gives you six hours, and Gold gives you eight, which means the photographer stays right through the evening party." },
{ s: 'B', t: "I'd love the Gold package, honestly. What does that one cost?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Gold is one thousand three hundred pounds. Silver is nine hundred and fifty." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Hmm. That's quite a difference, and we're already over budget on the catering. If the photographer is there from the ceremony until the speeches, would six hours be enough?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Easily. The speeches are usually over by about eight, and the first dance can be photographed in the same session. Most couples with a reception like yours choose Silver and are very happy with it." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Then I'll go with the Silver package, nine hundred and fifty pounds." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Wonderful. To secure the date we ask for a deposit of two hundred pounds, which comes off the total. The balance is due two weeks before the wedding." },
{ s: 'B', t: "That's fine. Do I pay by card?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Yes, I can take that over the phone once you've agreed the details, or you can do it through our secure payment page." },
{ s: 'B', t: "I'll do it through the website this evening. And how will we receive the photographs afterwards? Do we get prints?" },
{ s: 'A', t: "Everything is delivered in a private online gallery, which you and your guests can browse, download and share. It is usually ready about four weeks after the wedding. If you would like the pictures on a memory stick as well, that is an extra forty pounds, but most clients find the gallery is enough." },
{ s: 'B', t: "The gallery will be fine. We can always print our favourites ourselves." },
{ s: 'A', t: "Before the day, Ross likes to meet couples to talk through the schedule. He is usually free on Wednesday evenings, so I'll ask him to call you to arrange a time." },
{ s: 'B', t: "Thank you, Joanne. You've been really helpful." },
{ s: 'A', t: "It's a pleasure. I'll send a confirmation email today. Congratulations again, Mr Haldane, and I hope the weather is kind to you." },
],
